        "quiz_type": "single_choice",
        "question_type": "single_choice",
        "question_title": "A is \\(50\\\\% \\) more efficient than B. Working together, they complete a task in \\(12\\) days. In how many days can A alone complete the task?",
        "question_instruction": "Choose one correct option.",
        "explanation": "Let B's daily work rate be \\(r\\). Then A's rate is \\(\\frac{3r}{2}\\), and \\(\\frac{5r}{2}=\\frac{1}{12}\\). Thus A's rate is \\(\\frac{1}{20}\\), so A alone takes \\(20\\) days.",
        "question_audio": null,
        "time_limit_seconds": 30,
        "points": 10,
        "sort_order": 70,
        "question_data": {
